#     -A Specify section address.
#     -B Place bank info in .bnk file.
#     -C Specify CODE address.
#     -D Specify DATA address.
#     -E Place errors in a .err file.
#     -F Read arguments from the specified file.
#     -G Generate source debug information.
#     -H Specify the hex output format.
#     -J Sort module info by name.
#     -K Specify KDATA address.
#     -L Specify a library name.
#     -M Specify machine format.
#     -N Discard .QCK symbols.
#     -O Specify the name of the output file.
#     -P Set the fill characters in the hex output file.
#     -Q Tell the linker to be quiet.
#     -S Specify the symbol file format to use.
#     -T Generate a map file.
#     -U Specify UDATA address.
#     -V Display additional information.
#     -W Disable warnings.
#     -X Use EMM memory for symbol tables.
#     -Z Set the spread for the section.

# In WDC_Cstartup_816.asm, using "SECTION" allows mapping code the addresses below

#	ROM: 
#		FFF0 : 6502 emulation mode interrupt vectors (16 bytes) 
#		FFE0 : 65816 native mode interrupt vectors (16 bytes) 
#		FF00 : ISRs routines (RESET, IRQ, NMI, ABORT, BRK, etc) 
#		FE00 : STARTUP section in .asm file 
#		FA00 : WOZMON (if used) 
#		F900 : Some strings (name, date, etc) 
#		F000 : KDATA segment: constant data that never changes (strings/lookup table/...) 
#		8000 : CODE segment: main program section: main.c, .h and .c includes, ... 
#	RAM: 
# 		7F00 : XCS0 
# 		7F20 : XCS1 
# 		7F40 : XCS2 
# 		7F60 : XCS3 
# 		7F80 : ACIA (used for console terminal) 
# 		7FA0 : PIA 
# 		7FC0 : VIA 
# 		7FF0 : VIA2 
#		7EE0 : Shadow (currently not used / commented out) 
#		xxxx - 7DFF : main program stack 
#		2000 : DATA segment: initialized and changing variables 
#		1800 - 19FF : Wozmon data section 
#		1000 : 256 bytes of circular keyboard input buffer 

-AINPUT_BUFFER=1000 
-D2000 
-ASHADOW=7EE0 
-C8000 
-KF000 
-ASTRINGS=F900
#-AWOZMON=FA00 
-ASTARTUP=FE00 
-AISRS=FF00
-AVECTORS=FFE0 
-G  
-T 
-HI